--- PR #967 patch (before)
+++ rebased on candidate-54 (after)
@@ -1,37 +1,11 @@
-From 66b5b3e10231603235ae6e204e69dad123d7dc9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
-From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
-Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:43:05 +0000
-Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): vectorize TileLang reinterpret and merge
- read-state IfThenElse in sparse_mla
-
-Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 320021e3c4dbb202d911ab70e2cd924c75420488.
-
-Rationale:
-1. In sparse_mla.py, dequant_swa computes the UE8M0 scale via T.reinterpret(T.shift_left(T.cast(staged[i, D + d // SWA_GROUP], T.uint32), 23), accum_dtype). After DecoupleTypeCast stages the scale bytes into a thread-local array indexed by the vectorized loop variable vec, LegalizeVectorizedLoop invokes VectorizePlanner (src/transform/loop_vectorize.cc), which checks Op::GetAttrMap<TVectorizable>("TVectorizable"). Even though TLVectorizer::MutateReinterpretExpr_ already vectorizes builtin::reinterpret() across lanes, tirx.reinterpret is registered without TVectorizable = true, causing VectorizePlanner to reject loop-variant arguments inside reinterpret and fall back to a serial 8-iteration loop.
-2. In decode Stage 1 and Stage 2, IfStmtBinding distributes if seg_active(...) across every statement in SeqStmt because IsReplayableScalarBind allows CallEffectKind::kReadState conditions (reading SwaLengths and IdxLengths) when the body does not write to those buffers. However, MergeIfStmt only re-merges adjacent IfThenElse blocks when SideEffect(condition) <= CallEffectKind::kPure, leaving 10 split if blocks in Stage 1 and 6 split if blocks per unrolled segment (30 branches across 5 segments) in Stage 2.
-
-Register TVectorizable = True on tirx.reinterpret and wrap tilelang.transform.MergeIfStmt with a read-state IfThenElse merger that coalesces consecutive IfThenElse blocks (without else) sharing an identical read-only condition when intermediate statements do not write to any buffer or redefine any variable read by the condition.
-
-Quality:
-Bitwise-identical uint16 outputs across all sparse_mla routes (split, decode, extend). Eliminates all LegalizeVectorizedLoop serial-fallback warnings on sparse_mla, vectorizes dequant_swa into 2 x float4 iterations, collapses Stage 1+2 seg_active branches from 16 (30 unrolled in Stage 2) down to 3 (5 unrolled in Stage 2), and reduces decode (rows=8, H=40) latency by 5.2% median (17.28 us -> 16.39 us).
-
-Tests:
-- pytest --noconftest -p tests.kernels.deepseek_v41_pdl_sources tests/kernels/attention/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang.py -k "sparse_mla or wo_input" tests/kernels/attention/test_deepseek_v41_ced_replay.py (24 passed, 0 PDL violations across 2 boots).
-
-Upstream status: local runtime compiler pass activation paired with TileLang C++ patch 0014.
----
